const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文用逐笔层面的价格形成框架，询问信息冲击和微观结构摩擦如何共同影响日内价格变化。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"“Why Do Security Prices Change? A Transaction-Level Analysis of NYSE Stocks” frames a bounded research question. Read the stated question together with the named sample, dates, and institutional setting rather than treating it as a conclusion that automatically travels to another market or period."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/10.4.1035",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (1997) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (1997) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"来源构建并检验结构模型，分析日内买卖价差、波动、交易成本以及成交和报价自相关的模式。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"For “Why Do Security Prices Change? A Transaction-Level Analysis of NYSE Stocks”, the source describes a deliberate comparison, observation window, and control relation. Those choices are part of its research contract: changing one can change the proposition being tested, even when the method label remains the same."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/10.4.1035",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (1997) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (1997) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"需要逐笔成交、同步报价、交易方向、交易成本定义、日内分段和交易场所制度资料。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"For “Why Do Security Prices Change? A Transaction-Level Analysis of NYSE Stocks”, keep the fields, their availability timing, and the sample filters separate from the original study. A same-named variable, later-revised database, or matching end-of-period date is not automatically a comparable input."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/10.4.1035",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (1997) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (1997) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"摘要描述其用于理解价格发现与有效交易成本的度量；这些度量依赖交易与报价数据，而不是只依赖收盘价。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"For “Why Do Security Prices Change? A Transaction-Level Analysis of NYSE Stocks”, the source supports only the empirical or theoretical relation it describes. It does not turn association, model fit, or historical performance into causality, a directly executable procedure, or a guarantee about subsequent outcomes."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/10.4.1035",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (1997) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (1997) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"统一成交与报价时钟，明确有效价差和报价价差的定义，处理撤单、更正及开收盘竞价，并保存市场状态标签。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Before extending “Why Do Security Prices Change? A Transaction-Level Analysis of NYSE Stocks”, record its sample, timing, construction choices, and source edition in a versioned note. Keep the primary-source link and access date so a later reader can distinguish a changed definition from a changed result."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/10.4.1035",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (1997) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (1997) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Review of Financial Studies (1997)。该结构模型和原始 NYSE 制度不能被分钟蜡烛图复现，也不能自动给出另一场所的价格发现结论。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Review of Financial Studies (1997) for “Why Do Security Prices Change? A Transaction-Level Analysis of NYSE Stocks”. Its public description defines the boundary. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/10.4.1035",label:{zh:"Review of Financial Studies (1997) · 来源说明",en:"Review of Financial Studies (1997) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“Why Do Security Prices Change? A Transaction-Level Analysis of NYSE Stocks”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。该结构模型和原始 NYSE 制度不能被分钟蜡烛图复现，也不能自动给出另一场所的价格发现结论。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “Why Do Security Prices Change? A Transaction-Level Analysis of NYSE Stocks”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
